OL,3,AMahmood scraps settlement plans for
OL,4,Amigrant care workers
OL,5,
OL,6,FHome Secretary Shabana Mahmood has
OL,7,Fscrapped plans to make foreign care
OL,8,Fworkers already in the UK wait 15 years
OL,9,Fto qualify for permanent settlement.
OL,11,FMahmood had proposed doubling the wait
OL,12,Ffor indefinite leave to remain (ILR)
OL,13,Ffrom five years to 10 for most
OL,14,Fmigrants, with some facing a 15-year
OL,15,Fwait.
OL,17,FBut following a backlash from several
OL,18,FLabour MPs, Mahmood revised the policy
OL,19,Fand care workers who earn at least
OL,20,F#25,000 a year and arrived in the UK
OL,21,Fbefore May 2025 would continue to
OL,22,Fqualify after five years.
OL,23,APub: 02-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG3/39
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
